// What the demo page shows, generated by oci-agent-ui from ui/ui-spec.md.
// Every text is written for the customer persona, in the specification's
// language. Field names of the agent API appear only in `name` and `path`,
// never on the page.
//
// Shape:
// - language, title, story: page language, headline, one-sentence use case.
// - input.fields: what the user fills in; `name` is the request JSON field.
//   type: "textarea" | "text" | "number" | "select" (with options).
// - input.examples: one-click example requests (values for input.fields).
// - result.outcome: the most visible element; `path` reads the response,
//   `values` maps each value to a label and a tone (success | warning | info).
// - result.message: optional path of a business sentence from the agent.
// - result.fields: business fields shown in order; type "list" shows an array
//   as a small table with `columns`.
// - messages: plain-language texts for an invalid input, a rejected request
//   without its own message, and an unavailable service.
// - technicalView: false unless the developer asked for it explicitly.

